  "notes": "Curatorial planning tool for a civic art collection. Warm off-white background (#f4f3ef) with a near-black navy top bar, teal (#1f5f63) as the brand/primary, green for eligible/excellent, amber for warnings and stale condition checks. Distinctive encodings: two-letter space-code chips (RR/EA/CA) that are green when eligible, amber with warnings, grey struck-through when not eligible; star toggles for shortlist; 'Slot N' pill replaces the Propose button for works already in the proposal; proposal slots carry a coloured left rule (green ok, amber warning, dashed for open). Constraint checking is front-and-center: requirement lines with ✕, wall-length capacity meters, per-slot warnings. Row click opens a right overlay drawer with per-space fit calculations. The 'Collection register' top button swaps to a second view (register table with facet sidebar with counts and pagination) not in the capture."
